.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-payments - Payment lifecycle operations


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 payments [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage the full RAIL0 payment lifecycle.

.PP
Every on-chain operation is atomic: pass --private-key (-p) and the CLI prepares
the unsigned transaction, signs it locally, and broadcasts it in a single step.

.PP
rail0 payments authorize  -p 0xYourPrivateKey…

.PP
Authorize-and-capture flow:
  1. payments create -F 0xBuyer… -p 0xPayerKey…  — payer creates + signs
  2. payments authorize  -p 0xPayeeKey…  — payee authorizes
  3. payments capture    -a  -p 0xPayeeKey…  — payee captures

.PP
Charge (one-shot) flow:
  1. payments create -C -F 0xBuyer… -p 0xPayerKey…
  2. payments charge  -p 0xPayeeKey…


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for payments


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


